--- An explainer: { name, order (lower answers first; the agent's is 10), label, byline, run = fn(req) returning markdown }. req has kind, subject, context, files, depth and format (when set, the shape the answer must take instead of prose). It only answers: explaining changes nothing.
---@param spec table
function oriel.agent.explainer(spec) end

--- Asks a session's agent a side question, answered outside its conversation with no tools (the first forker's answer: the agent's is a fork of it): req { session (the session in front if omitted, else the newest open one), prompt, timeout (seconds, 180 by default) }. fn(answer, err, label) gets it on the loop; label says who answered: 'claude · fork, no tools'.
---@param req table
---@param fn function
function oriel.agent.fork(req, fn) end

--- A forker, which answers side questions for a session (btw, explain, the verify quiz): { name, order (lower answers first; the agent's is 10), label, run = fn(req) returning the answer }. req has session and prompt. It only answers, with no tools.
---@param spec table
function oriel.agent.forker(spec) end

--- A prompt pack: { prompt, tools }, for sessions to start with.
---@param name string
---@param spec table
function oriel.agent.pack(name, spec) end

--- Offer a tool to agents over MCP: { name, desc, params = { name = 'string' }, run = fn(p), read_only, reads, for = { 'assistant' }, confirm = fn(p), async, adds }. for names the agents it's for (session kinds, or the assistant); none is every session's. confirm makes it an act that waits for the user's yes: it returns { title, lead, rows = { { key, value, url } }, note, line }, and run's table { result, line, detail } says what was done. async gives run a second argument, done(result, err), to answer later: after a process or HTTP call. adds names another tool whose answer this one's result joins, under its reads, instead of being a tool of its own.
---@param spec table
function oriel.agent.tool(spec) end

---@class oriel.code
oriel.code = {}

--- A code host (GitLab, Azure DevOps…): where pull requests live. Oriel builds the Reviews page, the sidebar's pill, the notices and the assistant's review_requests on its review functions, and the Ship page's pull request step (raise, edit, ready, checks, merge) on the rest. { name, title, icon, order (50), words = { short ('PR', 'MR'), long ('pull request'), sigil ('#', '!') }, sites = { { host, api, secret, aliases } } its public servers (aliases: other hostnames its remotes use for one, its ssh hosts: 'ssh.dev.azure.com'), path = a regular expression over a git remote's path whose first group is the repo's name, takes = one over a pull request URL's path, shape = one over a whole remote URL that alone says a server is this host's (Azure DevOps' '/_git/'), setup = { api = 'https://{host}/api/v4', secret = 'GITLAB_TOKEN', token_url, token_help, probe = fn(host, done) answering true for a server of this host's, from a request that sends no token } for a server of your own, and the functions, each answering with done(value) or done(nil, err), now or later. A site is { host, api, secret }: a server you set up has its own secret, 'GITLAB_TOKEN:git.acme.corp', and the plugin is let reach it. Reviews, per site: requested = fn(site, done) with the open pull requests asking you, and those you're part way through; lookup = fn(site, url, done) with one in full; checkout = fn(site, url, done) with { remote, ref }: a substring of the registered repo's remote, and the refspec a review session fetches. Ship, each given repo = { session, project, remote, repo, site }: for_branch = fn(repo, branch, done) with the branch's pull request, open first, or nil; create = fn(repo, { title, body, branch, base, draft }, done); edit = fn(repo, pr, title, body, done); ready = fn(repo, pr, done); request_reviewers = fn(repo, pr, { logins }, done); checks = fn(repo, pr, done) with { { name, state ('ok', 'failed', 'running', 'queued', 'skipped'), url, started, completed, detail = a failing one's log line } }; merge_methods = fn(repo, pr, done) with { allowed = { 'merge', 'squash', 'rebase' }, default }; blockers = fn(repo, pr, done) with { { kind, count, text, hard = the host would refuse, url } }; merge = fn(repo, pr, { method, head, title, body, delete_branch }, done). Review mirroring: threads = fn(repo, pr, done) with { { id ('' or nil for the conversation), path, line, old, outdated, resolved, reviewer, state ('changes', 'approved', 'commented'), url, comments = { { id, author, body, at, member = the author belongs to the repo, so the agent may read it } } } }; reply = fn(repo, pr, thread = { id, path, line, old, url }, body, done) with the new comment's id, posting the draft the user forwards (thread.id empty: the conversation). Every answer crosses as JSON: an empty table is an empty list or object. A pull request is { number, id, title, body, url, author, state ('open', 'closed'), draft, merged, branch, base, head = its commit, reviewers }. A missing function's part isn't offered. A request is { url, repo, number, title, author, draft, asked (RFC 3339, or seconds since 1970), via (the team asked, '' for you), state ('new', 're-requested', 'changes', 'commented', 'approved'), since (commits since your review), adds, dels, files, ci ('ok', 'failed', 'running') }. A detail is { request, base, head, mergeable, labels = { names }, reviewers = { { login, state } }, body, files = { { path, adds, dels } }, checks, clone = the repo's clone URL, for Add repo… }.
---@param spec table
function oriel.code.host(spec) end

